My original question was

>       If I use my own account for PC-NFS login to get authentication, I
>       can mount disks on Ultrix machines.  If I use root for PC-NFS
>       login, I can mount disks on OSF1 machine.  But if I use my own
>       account for PC-NFS login, I can not mount disks on OSF1 machine.
>
>       Does OSF1 have some extra checking or security so to allow NFS
>       mount request only for root?

Many people pointed that I should have set /etc/rc.config file as the
following and that was collect. It solved the problem.

NONROOTMOUNTS=1

Best Regards,
Yoichi        Hi, OSF users

