> 
> I noticed that I have to have in the ~ftp/bin directory executables
> NOT dynamically linked (why can't you copy the /usr/shlib/*.so in
> ~ftp/usr/shlib directory so dynamically linked binaries can work ?)
> 
Answer from "Gernot M. Fuchs" <gfuchs@golay.med.unc.edu>:
For compress: start compress as ftp and check which dynamic libs you need and
copy them to the ftp home dir, too. The better solution however would be to
recompile compress with static libs.

> Anyway, the "ls" and "dir" commands are working *but* show the UID/GID
> for each file instead of real user and group (which are in ~ftp/etc/passwd
> and group of course) - any idea ?
> 
The documentation told to copy in ~ftp /etc/sia/siainitgood - you have
to copy the entire /etc/sia directory and everything works fine.

> Second, DU command "compress" is a dynamically linked binary. As I
> understood it should not work...is there a work around ?

Try to get the sources and compile with static option...

