From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Mar 20 01:33:21 1996
From: "Mark M. Van Overbeke" <markvo () cda ! mrs ! umn ! edu>
Date: Wed, 20 Mar 1996 01:33:21 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Seagate ST-12400 on Alpha
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076330121447

Thanks to those who gave me suggestions.  I think I had heard about the scu
utility, but that didn't enter my mind.  I will now have that stored away
for future reference.  I appears that my problem was "SCSI length" induced.
I had removed a couple of devices from the chain before I had tried getting
that drive working yesterday, but apparently that wasn't enough.  This time
I went right from the system box to the new drive and then to the others.  I
also replaced a couple of my cables with shorter versions.  I think I was
pushing the 3 meter length limit of the fast scsi on the AlphaStation.  I
might now be over by just a fraction.  I think I was at least 50% over
before the cable changes.  It sure would be nice to have another system here
I could try this stuff on without having to take down one of the main
systems to get stuff like this done.  Oh well, such is life I guess.
Everything went smooth this time with the scsi chain shortened.  A little
more thought may have prevented that problem in the first place, but I
learned a few things from the net that I wouldn't have had with the problem.
Thanks to all!!

