My original question was:

>We're running elm under DU 3.2.  The mail spool is on an DU 3.2 file system,
>and the mail spool directory has permissions rwxrwxrwt and each mail file
>has permissions rw-------.  When you exit elm with all the messages deleted,
>elm gives the "Problems restoring permissions of folder /var/spool/mail/user" 
>warning (it still keeps the empty folder with the correct permissions!).
>It's fine when you exit elm with at least one message.  We didn't have this 
>problem when the mail spool was on an Ultrix 4.2 file system.


I received three suggestions:

1. Upgrade elm. As a recall, it was a problem in elm fixed in new versions.

2. I had this same problem, and then I recompiled elm using all three
   file-locking methods there is available to configure. Works just fine 
   after that. We're running 3.2C

3. The symptoms could stem from the way you're locking the mailfiles. Try a
   'rcmgr set MAILLOCKING 5' and restart sendmail (also check the manpages 
   for mail_manual_setup).


I recompiled elm (V2.4, Patch 25) using all three file locking methods. And
the problem is gone.  I did try suggestion 3, but that didn't seem to solve
our problem.


