Subject: Summary:  Open3D Installation Problems
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076330121306

I had reported problems with the install of Open3D.  The answer seems to 
be simply that the extensions that were reported to be missing are 
not supported by the SVGA graphics card in our machine, so the 
source is a hardware error.  This was also the cause of the 
BLT engine hung in atiDrawColorImage GLOBALWAIT
errors that were filling up our xdm-errors file around this time.

lampert@alf.dec.com gives this information:
-------------------
GLX is an Xserver extention which is only available on the following
Digital Graphics cards...

zlxp-e series
zlxp-l series
zlx-m series.

Digital systems with ATI Mach64 and Compaq Qvision graphics cards
do not support GLX.  Most PC based Xservers and Xterminals don't either.

-------------------


Thanks to all who responded.

Steve Timm
SUNY Albany

