Subject: [SUMMARY} /dev/kmem
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96076330121261

Hi,

My question was " why did top suddenly stopped working?"

Knut Hellebo <Knut.Hellebo@nho.hydro.com> gave me the answer in a couple of 
seconds:

- the "/dev/kmem: permission denied" message was due to top not running suid
  (why did it lose the sticky bit?)

- to make top run again, I just had to recompile it (indeed, I'm running 
3.2c
  and it was compiled under 3.2)

Thanks Knut!

