        Thanks to all!  The basic view seems to be that I should focus on the 
"/" in the message (I was focusing on "/:", and wondering what kind of directory
that was rather than realizing the colon was punctuating the message 
text--duhhh...), and that most likely the tmp directory being mounted under / 
was what was filling up.  Apparently, it would get cleaned out shortly 
afterwards so that by the time we checked from elsewhere, "df" did not show 
anything full.  Since Oracle uses lots of tmp space during installs, we should 
either set one of its parameters to use space on another file system with more 
free space, or create tmp on another file system with more space. 

Again, thanks, and I will try to get a more complete summary together with due 
acknowledgements to all contributors...gotta run.

