12 digit hex number. My main concern was how to find the hostid if the lmhostid
program was not present.

Thanks to:
Richard Jackson
Olle Eriksson

>> It gets the number for the physical address -- Ethernet address.  Hostid
>> only has a value if you set it.

>> Then 12 char number from lmhostid is the ethernet hardware adress of
>> your networks card (or one of your cards)

My final solution is, if lmhostid is not on the system use uerf and look for
the Ethernet Interface address.

Thanks.

